</td><td align="center" valign="middle" style="border-bottom:solid thin" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Randomized, blinded crossover</td><td align="center" valign="middle" style="border-bottom:solid thin" rowspan="1" colspan="1">34.9 &#x000b1; 16.4<break/>(13&#x02013;60)</td><td align="center" valign="middle" style="border-bottom:solid thin" rowspan="1" colspan="1">8</td><td align="center" valign="middle" style="border-bottom:solid thin" rowspan="1" colspan="1">5:3</td><td align="center" valign="middle" style="border-bottom:solid thin" rowspan="1" colspan="1">OCD (<italic>n</italic> = 4), ADHD (<italic>n</italic> = 3)</td><td align="center" valign="middle" style="border-bottom:solid thin" rowspan="1" colspan="1">rTMS</td><td align="center" valign="middle" style="border-bottom:solid thin" rowspan="1" colspan="1">None</td><td align="center" valign="middle" style="border-bottom:solid thin" rowspan="1" colspan="1">L MC, L PFC</td><td align="center" valign="middle" style="border-bottom:solid thin" rowspan="1" colspan="1">Tic and OCD symptoms improved <underline>significantly</underline>.</td></tr><tr><td align="center" valign="middle" style="border-bottom:solid thin" rowspan="1" colspan="1">
